iness: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-03\nValid as Of: 2023-11-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3945 ---\nComponent: Data Attribute Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support for X.509 Authentication\nDescription: The Data Attribute Recommendation service now supports X.509 authentication.  See Enable X.509 Authentication.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-03\nValid as Of: 2023-11-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3946 ---\nComponent: SAP Alert Notification Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Custom Domain Warning Events are now supported\nDescription: You can now use the newly supported Custom Domain Warning Events.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-03\nValid as Of: 2023-11-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3947 ---\nComponent: SAP Alert Notification Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New SAP Credential Store event\nDescription: You can now use the newly supported Number Of Bindings Threshold Reached event.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-03\nValid as Of: 2023-11-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3948 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Other\nTitle: Root Certificate Replacement\nDescription: DigiCert has deprecated their DigiCert Global Root CA and will stop issuing certificates for SAP under any of its Intermediate CAs (ICA) at the end of 2023. For more information, see DigiCert root and intermediate CA certificate updates 2023.  SAP Cloud Identity Services switches to the G2 ICA and will deploy certificates signed by the new CA for the domains listed below starting in mid-November 2023. This means that the DigiCert Root CA domain certificate will be signed by DigiCert Global Root G2 instead of DigiCert Global Root CA. The following domains are affected:    *.accounts.ondemand.com      *.accounts.cloud.sap      *.accounts.sapcloud.cn      *.trial-accounts.ondemand.com      Action: If your SAP Cloud Identity Services tenants are running on any of the affected domains, ensure that you trust the new root CA: DigiCert Global Root G2.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-02\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3949 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Root Certificate Replacement\nDescription: DigiCert has deprecated their DigiCert Global Root CA and will stop issuing certificates for SAP under any of its Intermediate CAs (ICA) at the end of 2023. For more information, see DigiCert root and intermediate CA certificate updates 2023.      If your tenant is running on SAP BTP, Neo environment and you are using Identity Provisioning proxy and real-time provisioning scenarios, ensure that you trust the new root CA: DigiCert Global Root G2. It replaces the old one DigiCert Global Root CA.   For more information, see Root Certificate Replacement.      If your tenant is running on SAP Cloud Identity Services infrastructure on the domains listed below, ensure that you trust the new root CA: DigiCert Global Root G2 starting in mid-November 2023:      *.accounts.ondemand.com      *.accounts.cloud.sap      *.accounts.sapcloud.cn      *.trial-accounts.ondemand.com          For more information, see Root Certificate Replacement in What's New for Identity Authentication.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\n\",3337\n292,\"--- Record 2321 ---\nComponent: SAP Cloud Application Event Hub\nEnvironment: Other\nTitle: Support for IAS-based certificate authentication\nDescription: Use the SAP Cloud Identity service to manage certificates and authenticate the subscriber applications that share events with SAP Cloud Application Event Hub. See Authentication.\nAction: Inf